      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. Doses this high carry a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum). This is my best guess at a transposition or typo.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1000 mg.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
